  goldReward: 500
  expReward: 100
  offerDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - Now, this is your project.
    - I could suggest a bridge type or tell you where I'd place supports, but I want
      to see your solution.
    - Review the site and the contract requirements. Choose your design and materials,
      and consider how all the components work together.
    - <b><#E09500>Build and test under the required conditions, then use the results
      to identify any improvements</color></b>.
    - You've come a long way, {PlayerName}. Take your time and give this the thought
      it deserves. If you're ready, take the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - You know the requirements, {PlayerName}.
    - <b><#E09500>Take your time with the design and work through the test results
      carefully</color></b>.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Mills
    sentences:
    - Well, {PlayerName}. You did it.
    - When Clark first told me Professor Bhan's student was coming to Ironhaven,
      I was curious how you'd handle the projects here.
    - I've watched you work through the sites, test your designs, and make adjustments
      when things didn't go as planned.
    - This final bridge asked you to consider the requirements and make the decisions
      yourself.
    - 'That''s what I wanted to see: an engineer who studies the problem and works
      toward a solution.'
    - Good work, {PlayerName}. You've earned my respect.
